        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 26 at 12:58AM MDT until September 26 at 7:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Rapid river rises caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...North Central Guadalupe County in east central New
Mexico...

* WHEN...Until 700 AM MDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...River or stream flows are elevated in the Gallinas River
near Colonias and the Pecos River from near Dilia to near Santa
Rosa Lake State Park.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 1257 AM MDT, gauge reports indicated elevated flows in the
Gallinas River and Pecos River due to heavy rainfall on Friday.
Rapid river rises may cause minor flooding in the advisory area.
- Stay awake from river banks.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Colonias.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the
dangers of flooding.</instruction>
